for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob04re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Sentence Stress", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "Using stress in the pronunciation of sentences gives English its <span class=\"strong\">rhythm</span> or \"beat\".", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Word stress emphasizes <span class=\"strong\">one syllable</span> inside a <span class=\"strong\">word</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Sentence stress focuses on <span class=\"strong\">certain words</span> inside a <span class=\"strong\">sentence</span>.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "There are two basic types of words in most sentences: <br><br> <span class=\"strong\">Content Words</span> <ul><li>Content words are the key words of a sentence. They provide the meaning of the sentence. </li> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Structure Words</span> <ul><li>Structure words are not as important as content words. They are small words that you use to make the sentence correct. </li>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I would <span class=\"strong\">never</span> go back to <span class=\"strong\">work</span>!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"strong\">bet</span> he's got a <span class=\"strong\">few</span> stories.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "How <span class=\"strong\">terrifying</span>!", "type": "example"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "guard", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person whose job or duty it is to watch and protect someone or something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The guard locked the main doors of the building.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob04aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when telling a scary story.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to bet", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to be fairly confident that something is true or that something will probably happen", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I bet there are ghosts in that palace.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob04aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "menacing ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "possibly dangerous or threatening", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The menacing dog growled at the strangers.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob04aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "figure", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a person or animal that can be seen only as a shape or outline", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The dark figure stood in the doorway.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob04aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "corridor", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a long, narrow passage inside a building", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We walked down the dark corridor.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob04aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to drag", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to go or move more slowly than others", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The tired man dragged his body down the hall.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob04aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to haunt", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a place visited or lived in by a ghost ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A ghost haunts the north tower.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob04aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "footsteps", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a sound made by your foot as you walk or run ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I could hear footsteps behind me.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob04aud08", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to paralyze", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to make a person unable to move ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The tourist was paralyzed with fear.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob04aud09", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to lock up", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to lock the door or gate", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The guard locked up.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le03ob04aud10", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Write a ghost story using 80-100 words.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Include a lot of detail to make your story interesting!", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Consider the characters, the setting and the plot.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use paragraph structure.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your ghost story to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write a ghost story.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I include characters, a setting and a plot.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I use paragraph structure.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I read my ghost story to a partner.", "type": "text"}]}]}